ralph/progress.txt:205:- Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **project-scoped preview lifecycle table whose row points at both a preview-kind environment clone and a source environment, carries soft-delete lifecycle state, and exposes Insert + GetByID + ListByProject + Update + ScheduleDeletion + DeleteByID** (BE-0479 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/preview_environment_repository_invariants_test.go for preview_environments). The table is tenant-scoped by direct `(organization_id, project_id)` predicates and composite FKs to `environments (organization_id, project_id, id)`, uses `penv_` IDs via `domain.KindPreviewEnvironment`, and adds a trigger to enforce that the wrapped environment row has `kind='preview'` because a FK cannot express referenced-row-body predicates. It keeps status/deletion state out of customer metadata Update, and uses ScheduleDeletion (`status='deleting'`, `deletion_scheduled_at=COALESCE(..., now())`) for API teardown while preserving hard DeleteByID for worker cleanup after Dokploy teardown. Forward-applicable to future project-scoped lifecycle rows that wrap a concrete hierarchy resource with worker-owned status: test row shape/default status, deterministic `(created_at,id)` list ordering, optimistic conflicts, soft-delete lifecycle, hard-delete cleanup, constraint conflicts, referenced-row-body trigger conflicts, rollback, nil-Tx guards, and database-owned version/timestamps.
