+- What was implemented: Added the production rollback checklist artifact and static release contract. The checklist covers API/worker binary coupling, Customer / Agent / CI -> Yalla API -> Postgres source of truth -> provisioning worker -> private Dokploy API boundary, least-privilege operator-managed config, rollback decision gates, backup and restore rehearsal prechecks, migration rollback safety through `/usr/local/bin/yalla-api --migrate-only`, health/readiness/version/metrics probes, structured log redaction, durable job/dead-letter checks, and opt-in external Dokploy smoke guidance.
+- Files changed: `docs/operations/rollback-checklist.md`, `internal/release/rollback_checklist_artifact_static_test.go`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `scripts/verify.sh`, `SECURITY.md`, `internal/release/AGENTS.md`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
+- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `goimports -w .` attempted but `goimports` is not installed; `go mod tidy`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./internal/release/... -run TestRollbackChecklistArtifact`; `golangci-lint run ./...`; strict pre-commit `scripts/verify.sh --strict --release` also ran focused verification suites, `govulncheck ./...`, `staticcheck ./...`, `goreleaser check`, and `goreleaser release --snapshot --clean`.
+- Results: Required formatting, module tidy, full tests, race detector, vet, focused rollback artifact static test, installed optional lint, vulnerability scan, static analysis, and snapshot release build passed. `goimports` is not installed in this environment.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups: No runtime API or persistence behavior changed. Future rollback operational implementation should keep the checklist, SECURITY gate row, CI step, verify step, and static test synchronized.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Operations runbook/checklist artifacts in `internal/release` are pinned by static tests that assert the docs, SECURITY.md, CI, and `scripts/verify.sh` together; add the failing static test first so missing surfaces are obvious.
+  - Keep required static-test phrases contiguous in Markdown; line wrapping can break `strings.Contains` checks even when the prose is semantically present.
